# Ignore list for services/ukun-gateway/Dockerfile. BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in
# preference to a .dockerignore at the context root, which is how each service keeps its own
# list even though they all share the repository root as build context.

# Build output — the image compiles from source, it never copies a locally built jar. `**/build/`
# only matches directories named exactly `build`, so neither buildSrc/ nor any build.gradle.kts is
# caught by it.
**/build/
.gradle/

# Git metadata. In a worktree .git is a file, not a directory; both patterns are covered.
.git
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Secrets. .env.example is the versioned template and is not needed in the image either. The `**/`
# is what reaches apps/ukun-web/.env.development: a bare `.env.*` only matches the context root.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Everything outside the new services. `apps/` is NOT on this list, unlike in the other two images:
# this is the service that serves the SPA (skill `spring-gateway` §6), so its `web` stage builds
# apps/ukun-web from this same context. Removing it here would not break the build loudly — the
# COPY would fail outright, which is the good outcome; the bad one is adding it back later to "tidy
# up" and shipping a gateway whose fallback answers 404 on every page.
resources/
scripts/
docs/
.claude/
tilt_modules/
Tiltfile
compose*.yaml
*.md

# Of apps/ukun-web, what the build does not read. e2e/ and playwright.config.ts stay in: `npm run
# build` runs `tsc -b`, and tsconfig.json references tsconfig.e2e.json. These are their outputs, and
# they would invalidate the layer cache on every local smoke run.
apps/ukun-web/playwright-report/
apps/ukun-web/test-results/
apps/ukun-web/blob-report/

# The other projects' sources. Their build scripts are still needed to configure the build and are
# copied explicitly by the Dockerfile, so only src/ is excluded here. :ukun-test-support carries the
# shared ArchUnit rules and is never on a runtime classpath, so none of its sources belong in any
# image either.
services/ukun-api/src/
services/ukun-auth/src/
test-support/ukun-test-support/src/

# Frontend and IDE noise. The three `**/` prefixes are load-bearing since apps/ is in the context:
# a bare `node_modules/` only matches the context root, so the host's glibc node_modules would ride
# into an Alpine image and the `npm ci` of the web stage would be overwritten by it — the same
# failure apps/ukun-web/.dockerignore documents for the dev image, one layer over.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
